<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The company's four cues, as original audio.

  Owner direction, 2026-10-06: "a audio folder! sounds dope!!! how do we do sounds can we?", and
  the full reversal of the existing-content-only policy that answered it. These four shipped once
  in 0.2.0, were retired by the 2026-09-28 direction, and are reinstated by the 2026-10-06 one.
  See docs/CONTENT_REUSE_POLICY.md, which keeps both directions on the record.

  EVERY ONE OF THESE IS POSITIONAL, AND THREE OF THEM WERE NOT BEFORE.
  All ten call sites in RimroomsAudio.Play hand it a map and a cell. While the cues resolved to
  Core interface sounds (Message_ThreatSmall, CommsWindow_Open, Message_NegativeEvent) that
  position was passed in and thrown away, because an interface sound plays at the camera. Ours are
  MapOnly with a distRange, so a gate warning comes from the gate and a spatial tell comes from the
  pawn who noticed it. A player who hears a warning and cannot tell which gate raised it has been
  given a noise rather than information.

  THE CORE SOUNDS REMAIN AS THE FALLBACK AND THAT IS DELIBERATE. RimroomsAudio resolves this def
  first and drops to the Core cue if it is missing or incompatible, so a package stripped of its
  Sounds folder degrades to the 0.12.x behaviour instead of falling silent.

  distRange is read as (full volume within, inaudible beyond). 12~55 is the 0.2.0 figure and is
  kept: a gate's working area is a room or two, and 55 cells reaches the next building without
  carrying across a map.
-->
<Defs>

  <SoundDef>
    <defName>RR_GatePowerRise</defName>
    <context>MapOnly</context>
    <maxVoices>1</maxVoices>
    <maxSimultaneous>1</maxSimultaneous>
    <subSounds>
      <li>
        <grains>
          <li Class="AudioGrain_Clip"><clipPath>Rimrooms/RR_GatePowerRise</clipPath></li>
        </grains>
        <volumeRange>35~35</volumeRange>
        <pitchRange>1~1</pitchRange>
        <distRange>12~55</distRange>
      </li>
    </subSounds>
  </SoundDef>

  <SoundDef>
    <defName>RR_GateWarning</defName>
    <context>MapOnly</context>
    <maxVoices>1</maxVoices>
    <maxSimultaneous>1</maxSimultaneous>
    <subSounds>
      <li>
        <grains>
          <li Class="AudioGrain_Clip"><clipPath>Rimrooms/RR_GateWarning</clipPath></li>
        </grains>
        <volumeRange>50~50</volumeRange>
        <pitchRange>1~1</pitchRange>
        <distRange>12~55</distRange>
      </li>
    </subSounds>
  </SoundDef>

  <SoundDef>
    <defName>RR_FieldRadio</defName>
    <context>MapOnly</context>
    <maxVoices>1</maxVoices>
    <maxSimultaneous>1</maxSimultaneous>
    <subSounds>
      <li>
        <grains>
          <li Class="AudioGrain_Clip"><clipPath>Rimrooms/RR_FieldRadio</clipPath></li>
        </grains>
        <volumeRange>35~35</volumeRange>
        <pitchRange>1~1</pitchRange>
        <distRange>12~55</distRange>
      </li>
    </subSounds>
  </SoundDef>

  <SoundDef>
    <defName>RR_SpatialTell</defName>
    <context>MapOnly</context>
    <maxVoices>1</maxVoices>
    <maxSimultaneous>1</maxSimultaneous>
    <subSounds>
      <li>
        <grains>
          <li Class="AudioGrain_Clip"><clipPath>Rimrooms/RR_SpatialTell</clipPath></li>
        </grains>
        <volumeRange>35~35</volumeRange>
        <pitchRange>1~1</pitchRange>
        <distRange>12~55</distRange>
      </li>
    </subSounds>
  </SoundDef>

</Defs>
